  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q8-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Given $\\cot\\theta=-\\frac{24}{7}$ for $-\\frac{\\pi}{2}<\\theta<\\frac{\\pi}{2}$, find:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 2,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sec\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac{25}{24}$",
          "worked": "The interval and $\\cot\\theta<0$ place $\\theta$ in quadrant IV, where cosine is positive. A reference triangle has adjacent side $24$ and opposite side $7$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}h&=\\sqrt{24^2+7^2}\\\\h&=25\\\\\\sec\\theta&=\\frac{\\mathrm{Hyp}}{\\mathrm{Adj}}\\\\\\sec\\theta&=\\frac{25}{24}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 37
      },
      {
        "id": "p13-q8-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\sin\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{7}{25}$",
          "worked": "In quadrant IV, sine is negative. Using the reference triangle with opposite side $7$ and hypotenuse $25$,\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin\\theta&=-\\frac{\\mathrm{Opp}}{\\mathrm{Hyp}}\\\\\\sin\\theta&=-\\frac{7}{25}.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
